      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "i believe this request could use a little note justifying why it's NEEDED:\n\nwhenever you visit worlds that require (or at least encourage) everyone to be in the same space, like various minigolf ones, Geolocator, color clues, or some museum-like worlds, the other players being right in our faces and covering our screens becomes a serious issue even for the most cuddly ones of us.\n\nif they were random people, the Personal Space feature would be a great solution, but sadly those worlds are in my experience mostly visited/played with friends, and this functionality... surprisingly just doesn't work on friends!\n\nnow, i would've understood if nobody thought of this functionality at all in the first place, but i think it's crazy that the \"on\" state works the way to does now.\n\nplease, make it a 3-way toggle of off/non-friends/everyone, or - if that's a problem for some reason - just make it work on friends as well (for now). i'm quite certain that this way it will cover more cases for using this functionality than the current state.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
